.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt CONF_MODULES_FREE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm CONF_modules_free ,
.Nm CONF_modules_finish ,
.Nm CONF_modules_unload
.Nd OpenSSL configuration cleanup functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/conf.h
.Ft void
.Fo CONF_modules_finish
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo CONF_modules_unload
.Fa "int all"
.Fc
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 1.1.0, and
can be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft void
.Fo CONF_modules_free
.Fa void
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn CONF_modules_free
closes down and frees up all memory allocated by all configuration
modules.
Normally, in versions of OpenSSL prior to 1.1.0, applications called
.Fn CONF_modules_free
at exit to tidy up any configuration performed.
.Pp
.Fn CONF_modules_finish
calls each configuration modules
.Sy finish
handler to free up any configuration that module may have performed.
.Pp
.Fn CONF_modules_unload
finishes and unloads configuration modules.
If
.Fa all
is set to
.Sy 0
only modules loaded from DSOs will be unloads.
If
.Fa all
is
.Sy 1
all modules, including built-in modules will be unloaded.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
None of the functions return a value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr config 5 ,
.Xr OPENSSL_config 3 ,
.Xr CONF_modules_load_file_ex 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn CONF_modules_free
was deprecated in OpenSSL 1.1.0; do not use it.
For more information see
.Xr OPENSSL_init_crypto 3 .
